      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wrote a small program to test this interesting idea and found that iter is moved at the 1st call to step_by(2) and thus the 2nd call to step_by(2) leads to an \u0027use of moved value\u0027 error. To make this works, we have to clone 1st iterator as below:\n\nfor (key, val) in std::iter::zip(iter.clone().step_by(2), iter.skip(1).step_by(2)) {...}\n\nCloning an iterator in this case might cost more than an unwrap, so I prefer to keep the original implementation. Thanks.",
